From b58d81ec54bd9de41f521b90d773d3b5cd6610bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 7 Mar 2026 13:51:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: abort ROC on chanctx changes

[ upstream commit 42955db08adf5979f56abc9ee4f0ad9a73b2aa4a ]

mt76_change_chanctx() calls mt76_phy_update_channel() which switches
the hardware channel. If ROC is active on the same phy, this switches
away from the ROC channel and clears offchannel, but leaves ROC state
intact. Mac80211 still thinks the phy is on the ROC channel.

Abort any active ROC before proceeding, matching the pattern already
used in add, remove, assign, unassign, and switch chanctx functions.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Backport-note: context only. The SDK traces the change with mt76_phy_dbg()
 in mt76_change_chanctx(), so the ROC abort goes after that line and before
 mac_work is cancelled.
---
 channel.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/channel.c b/channel.c
index d44245b6..af4ac7c4 100644
--- a/channel.c
+++ b/channel.c
@@ -99,6 +99,9 @@ void mt76_change_chanctx(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	mt76_phy_dbg(phy, "change to %u, 0x%x", conf->def.chan->hw_value, changed);
 
+	if (phy->roc_vif)
+		mt76_abort_roc(phy);
+
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&phy->mac_work);
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mutex);
-- 
